cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Threshold generalisation across care settings and hospitals for ECG-AI diagnostic support
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abbou
    given-names: Ruben
repository-code: https://github.com/rabbou/ecg-conformal-shift
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Measures the share of ill patients an ECG model's decision threshold
  recognises once it leaves the population it was set on. On EchoNext,
  thresholds fitted on Columbia inpatients are read on outpatients for three
  models, beside the AUROC, the severity of disease and the local labels that
  refit them; an infarction model is carried from PTB-XL to two Chinese
  hospitals, and five corpora take the calibration role in turn on five
  rhythm and conduction diagnoses. Each threshold is read as a sensitivity
  threshold and as the per-class conformal rule that adds a referral band.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - electrocardiography
  - structural heart disease
  - myocardial infarction
  - distribution shift
  - class-conditional coverage
